@import net.keyboardbuilders.keyboardbuilders.web.Head
@import net.keyboardbuilders.keyboardbuilders.web.SiteUrl
@param head: Head
@param site: SiteUrl
@param content: gg.jte.Content
@param wide: Boolean = false
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <title>${head.title} · Keyboard Builders</title>
    @if(head.description != null)
        <meta name="description" content="${head.description}">
    @endif
    <%--
        CANONICAL AND NOINDEX ARE NEVER BOTH PRESENT, and `Head` is where that is decided
        rather than here. They contradict each other: `noindex` says drop this page,
        `canonical` says fold it into another one. Given both, a crawler picks one and
        which one is not defined.
    --%>
    @if(head.canonical != null)
        <link rel="canonical" href="${head.canonical}">
    @endif
    @if(!head.indexable)
        <meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow">
    @endif
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="${site.stylesheet}">
    <%-- THE TAB ICON. Three files and each earns its place: the SVG carries its own
         prefers-color-scheme rule so it follows the reader's theme like the rest of the
         site; the .ico is the fallback, in a MID grey with the terracotta top key,
         because a raster has no theme and must stay legible on light and dark tab
         chrome alike; the PNG is for iOS, which composites onto an opaque tile and so
         needs a ground -- the header bar's own dark.

         The .ico's 16px layer is drawn on the pixel grid rather than scaled down from
         the vector, which is the whole reason a raster fallback is worth shipping: the
         same four keys scaled to 16 blur into a smudge, and hinted they stay four keys. --%>
    <%-- THE RASTER IS DECLARED UNDER PLAIN `rel="icon"`, and both halves of that matter
         to a crawler rather than to a browser. Google's favicon crawler reads the rel
         values `icon`, `shortcut icon`, `apple-touch-icon` and
         `apple-touch-icon-precomposed` -- `alternate icon` is not one of them -- and it
         decodes BMP, GIF, ICO, PNG, JPEG, PPM and TIFF, which does not include SVG. So
         the previous head offered it a rel it reads pointing at a format it cannot, and
         a format it can under a rel it does not.

         Browsers are unaffected and still take the SVG: it is declared second with an
         explicit `type`, and a browser picks the best format it understands rather than
         the first link it sees. Owner-reported after a Google result for "reviung53"
         showed the generic globe. --%>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32 48x48">
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml">
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png">
    <%-- THE NAME A HOME-SCREEN INSTALL OFFERS. Without these a phone suggests the page
         title, which on the front page is "Home · Keyboard Builders". Android reads the
         manifest, iOS the apple meta, and the rest fall back to application-name. --%>
    <link rel="manifest" href="/site.webmanifest">
    <meta name="application-name" content="Keyboard Builders">
    <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Keyboard Builders">
    <%-- OPEN GRAPH. This hobby lives on Discord and r/ErgoMechKeyboards, which is exactly
         where a link gets pasted, and without these a paste previews as a bare URL.

         The same title and description the search result uses, so there is ONE set of
         words to keep true rather than two drifting apart.

         The card is drawn, not photographed -- `OgImageController` renders the design's
         own silhouette into a 1200x630 raster, since Open Graph wants a raster and ours
         is inline SVG sized for a 40px row. --%>
    <meta property="og:type" content="website">
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Keyboard Builders">
    <meta property="og:title" content="${head.title}">
    @if(head.image != null)
        <meta property="og:image" content="${head.image}">
        <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200">
        <meta property="og:image:height" content="630">
        <meta name="twitter:image" content="${head.image}">
    @endif
    <%-- `summary_large_image` only where there IS one; the plain `summary` card is right
         for a page whose picture would be a list. --%>
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="@if(head.image != null)summary_large_image@else summary@endif">
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="${head.title}">
    @if(head.description != null)
        <meta property="og:description" content="${head.description}">
        <meta name="twitter:description" content="${head.description}">
    @endif
    @if(head.canonical != null)
        <meta property="og:url" content="${head.canonical}">
    @endif
    <%-- SCHEMA.ORG, not og:image again. Forgejo #42: Google indexes an `<img src>` or a
         `primaryImageOfPage`, and this page has neither -- its only images are two
         inline `<svg>`, which are markup, not an indexed resource. `og:image` is a
         1200x630 card with a wordmark, which Google's own guidance says to avoid
         ("a generic image, for example your site logo"); the thumbnail is the
         silhouette alone, square, drawn for exactly this. --%>
    @if(head.thumbnail != null)
        <%-- Built by JsonLd, not templated: jte escapes for JavaScript inside a script, and
             its \- in every hyphenated slug is not JSON. --%>
        <script type="application/ld+json">$unsafe{head.webPageLd ?: ""}</script>
    @endif
</head>
<body>
<header class="site">
    <%-- THE MARK, INLINE AND NOT AN img, so it inherits currentColor and needs no second
         file for the dark theme. Four keys stepped into a column stagger: pinky lowest,
         middle finger furthest, index back down. The same four rects are in
         static/favicon.svg and MarkTest asserts the two agree. --%>
    <a class="wordmark" href="/">
        <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="20" height="20" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
            <g fill="currentColor">
                <rect x="1.4" y="18.4" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                <rect x="9.1" y="13" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                <rect x="16.8" y="7.2" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                <rect x="24.5" y="11.2" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
            </g>
        </svg>
        <span>keyboardbuilders</span>
    </a>
    <nav class="bar-links"><a href="/designs">Designs</a> <a href="/favorites">Favorites</a> <a href="/settings">Settings</a></nav>
    <%-- THE SAME LINKS BEHIND A MENU on a narrow screen, where they wrapped onto a second
         line (owner, 2026-10-02). A details element, so it opens without JavaScript;
         app.css shows exactly one of the two. --%>
    <details class="menu">
        <summary aria-label="Menu">&#9776;</summary>
        <nav><a href="/designs">Designs</a> <a href="/favorites">Favorites</a> <a href="/settings">Settings</a></nav>
    </details>
    <%-- CLOSED BY A TAP OUTSIDE IT OR BY ESCAPE, as a menu is expected to (reader-reported,
         2026-10-04). `pageshow` closes it too: Back restores a page from the cache with the
         menu still open from the link that left it. --%>
    <script>
        (function () {
            var menu = document.currentScript.previousElementSibling;
            document.addEventListener("pointerdown", function (e) {
                if (menu.open && !menu.contains(e.target)) menu.open = false;
            });
            document.addEventListener("keydown", function (e) {
                if (e.key === "Escape" && menu.open) {
                    menu.open = false;
                    menu.querySelector("summary").focus();
                }
            });
            window.addEventListener("pageshow", function () { menu.open = false; });
        })();
    </script>
</header>
<%-- `wide` is for scanning surfaces only -- 52rem stays right for a page of prose.
     `ResultsGridTest` holds that line. --%>
<main class="${if (wide) "wide" else null}">
    ${content}
</main>
<%-- THE FOOTER, deepened 2026-10-02 (owner): every link the top bar has, plus the site's
     own pages, so a reader at the bottom of a long page need not scroll back up. Column
     labels are plain text, not headings, so they stay out of each page's outline. --%>
<footer class="site-foot">
    <div class="foot-grid">
        <div class="foot-brand">
            <a class="foot-mark" href="/">
                <svg class="mark" viewBox="0 0 32 32" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                    <g fill="currentColor">
                        <rect x="1.4" y="18.4" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                        <rect x="9.1" y="13" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                        <rect x="16.8" y="7.2" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                        <rect x="24.5" y="11.2" width="6.4" height="6.4" rx="1.5"/>
                    </g>
                </svg>
                <span>keyboardbuilders</span>
            </a>
            <p>A searchable catalog of open-source keyboard designs, read from their own files.</p>
            <p>Made by <a class="external" href="https://fowlie.github.io" rel="noopener" target="_blank">fowlie<svg class="ext" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6"/><path d="M20 4 10 14"/><path d="M18 14v5a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5"/></svg></a> in Norway 🇳🇴</p>
        </div>
        <nav class="foot-col" aria-label="Browse">
            <p class="foot-label">Browse</p>
            <a href="/designs">Designs</a>
            <a href="/learn">Learn</a>
            <a href="/favorites">Favorites</a>
            <a href="/settings">Settings</a>
        </nav>
        <nav class="foot-col" aria-label="About">
            <p class="foot-label">About</p>
            <a href="/about">About this site</a>
            <a href="/about#privacy">Privacy</a>
            <a href="/account">Designers: sign in</a>
            <a href="mailto:hello@keyboardbuilders.net?subject=keyboardbuilders">hello@<wbr>keyboardbuilders.net</a>
            <%-- AGPL §13 asks a site running AGPL code to offer its source; every page does. --%>
            <a class="source-link external" href="https://github.com/fowlie/keyboardbuilders" rel="noopener" target="_blank"><svg class="gh" viewBox="0 0 16 16" width="13" height="13" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M8 0c4.42 0 8 3.58 8 8a8.013 8.013 0 0 1-5.45 7.59c-.4.08-.55-.17-.55-.38 0-.27.01-1.13.01-2.2 0-.75-.25-1.23-.54-1.48 1.78-.2 3.65-.88 3.65-3.95 0-.88-.31-1.59-.82-2.15.08-.2.36-1.02-.08-2.12 0 0-.67-.22-2.2.82-.64-.18-1.32-.27-2-.27-.68 0-1.36.09-2 .27-1.53-1.03-2.2-.82-2.2-.82-.44 1.1-.16 1.92-.08 2.12-.51.56-.82 1.28-.82 2.15 0 3.06 1.86 3.75 3.64 3.95-.23.2-.44.55-.51 1.07-.46.21-1.61.55-2.33-.66-.15-.24-.6-.83-1.23-.82-.67.01-.27.38.01.53.34.19.73.9.82 1.13.16.45.68 1.31 2.69.94 0 .67.01 1.3.01 1.49 0 .21-.15.45-.55.38A7.995 7.995 0 0 1 0 8c0-4.42 3.58-8 8-8Z"/></svg>Source code<svg class="ext" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6"/><path d="M20 4 10 14"/><path d="M18 14v5a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5"/></svg></a>
        </nav>
        <div class="foot-col">
            <p class="foot-label">Support</p>
            <a class="support-link external" href="https://ko-fi.com/keyboardbuilders" rel="noopener" target="_blank">Buy me a beer 🍺<svg class="ext" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="11" height="11" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M14 4h6v6"/><path d="M20 4 10 14"/><path d="M18 14v5a1 1 0 0 1-1 1H5a1 1 0 0 1-1-1V7a1 1 0 0 1 1-1h5"/></svg></a>
            <span class="foot-fine">or share the site with a friend</span>
        </div>
    </div>
</footer>
<%--
    Page views. Forgejo #27, amended: the counter moved from self-hosted to goatcounter.com
    on the owner's rule that nothing is self-hosted unless it has to be. The origin is
    configuration and UNSET LOADS NOTHING, so only the deployed instance counts anything.

    THE SECOND SCRIPT ON THE SITE, and the first that serves the operator rather than the
    reader -- #27 draws that distinction and it is a fair one. The no-JS alternative is
    GoatCounter's 1x1 pixel, which was measured and rejected on cost rather than
    principle: `p` is mandatory (the endpoint 400s without it), so a pixel needs the path
    threaded through this layout and every call site, plus the incoming Referer read in
    the controller if referrers are wanted. This tag needs one line and answers both
    halves of the launch question -- is anyone arriving, and from where.

    Blockers catch both roughly equally: filter lists match hostnames containing
    `goatcounter` and `/count` paths, so the pixel's only real gain is true `noscript`
    readers. If the numbers ever look implausibly low against another signal, switch to
    the pixel then, with this as the baseline to compare against.

    SELF-HOSTED, so first-party: no third-party request, and the same instance that
    stores the data serves the script.

    `async` so it never blocks render. The index is 85% inline SVG and the parse cost is
    the page's real expense (ux.md); this must not add to it.
--%>
@if(site.hasAnalytics)
    <script data-goatcounter="${site.analyticsOrigin}/count"
            async src="${site.analyticsScript}"></script>
@endif
</body>
</html>
